          "type": "text",
          "text": "WRITING HANDOUT \nTASK 1 – MULTIPLE CHARTS\nQuestion 1: The chart below shows the results of a survey about people's coffee and tea buying and drinking habits in five Australian cities.\nSummarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.\nQuestion 2: The tables below show sales of Fairtrade*-labelled coffee and bananas in five countries in Europe in 1999 and 2004.\n*Fairtrade: a category of products for which farmers from developing countries have been paid an officially agreed fair price.\nQuestion 3: The graphs below show how much water was used globally from 1900 to 2000 as well as in Brazil and Congo in 2000. Summarize the graphs by selecting and reporting the main features and make comparison where relevant\nQuestion 4: The chart below shows what Anthropology graduates from one university did after finishing their undergraduate degree courses. Summarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.\nQuestion 5: The chart shows export values of one country by category for 2015-2016. The table shows percentage changes between these years. Summarise the main features and make comparisons.\nQuestion 6: The two bar charts below show the proportion of 14- to 16-year-old students studying a foreign language in an English speaking country, and the top three foreign languages. Summarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.\nQuestion 6: The charts below give information on the location and types of dance classes young people in a town in Australia are currently attending. Summarize the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant."
        }
